#!/bin/sh
# Sound and Bluetooth audio: what the sound server, the ALSA cards and
# bluetoothd have, once a minute for 15 min (connect the headset and play
# something meanwhile). The server's own messages are in syslog-copy.log.
u() {
	timeout 10 su user -s /bin/sh -c "XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/run/user/1000 $*" 2>&1
}
(
	sleep 60
	# AudioReach card: PCMs from the topology, routing controls for UCM
	cat /proc/asound/cards /proc/asound/pcm
	amixer -c 0 controls 2>&1 | grep -E -i 'Audio Mixer|MultiMedia|RDAC|aw87|Speaker'
	for i in $(seq 15); do
		echo "== $(date '+%T') uptime $(cut -d' ' -f1 /proc/uptime)"
		ps -o pid,user,args | grep -E 'pulse|pipewire|wireplumber|bluetoothd|callaudiod|modem-daemon|telephony-daemon' | grep -v grep
		aplay -l 2>&1
		u pactl info
		u pactl list short sinks
		u pactl list short sink-inputs
		u pactl list cards
		for d in $(timeout 5 bluetoothctl devices Connected 2>/dev/null | cut -d' ' -f2); do
			timeout 5 bluetoothctl info "$d"
		done
		sync
		sleep 60
	done
) >/var/log/tapas-audio.log 2>&1 &
